\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1  (void)\b setTitleWidth:\b0 (float)\i width\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 You usually won\'27t need to to invoke this method, since the Application Kit automatically sets the title width whenever the title changes. If, however, the automatic width doesn\'27t suit your needs, you can use \b setTitleWidth:\b0  to set the width in pixels.\
\fs14\
\fs28 Once you have set the width explicity this way, the Application Kit stops setting the width automatically; you will need to invoke \b setTitleWidth:\b0  every time the title changes. If you want the Application Kit to resume automatic width assignments, invoke \b setTitleWidth:\b0  with a negative \i width\i0  value.\
\fs14\
